  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 429.78 K, melting point of In; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 0.780$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.647 + 0.182 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.810 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.647\\times10^{-3}T+0.091\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.810\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.858$ \nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-429.78 K: $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = 40.245 + 2.412 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 4.923 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 141.100 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 40.245 - 2.412 \\times 10^{-3} T \\ln T + 4.923 \\times 10^{-6} T^{2} + 70.550 T^{-1} - 4.496 \\times 10^{-3} T$ \n429.78-2000 K: $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = 40.605 - 1.935 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.150 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 75.400 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 40.605 + 1.935 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.150 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 37.700 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 29.461 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
